TITLE:: DrumProgrammer
SUMMARY:: Drum-machine step grid with looping playback.
CATEGORIES:: GUI>Views
RELATED:: Classes/AmpCommand, Classes/CommandPrompt, Classes/DrumStep, Classes/EnhancedButton, Classes/GridSlider, Classes/GuiPalette, Classes/PlayableNote, Classes/SCViewHolder, Classes/ScrollView, Classes/SequencePlayer, Classes/StaticText, Classes/SwitchCommand, Classes/View, Classes/Window

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::DrumProgrammer:: is a LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder:: that shows a grid of step squares on a LINK::Classes/GuiPalette:: colour1 background. Sound names and MIDI note numbers are held in a class LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: for now. It opens with one row of 16 squares for each sound, ordered by MIDI note number ascending from top to bottom: Kick 2 (35), Kick 1 (36), Rim (37), Snare (38), Clap (39), Tom 1 (41), Closed hi-hat (42), Tom 2 (43), Open hi-hat (46), Cymbal (49), Ride (51), Cowbell (56). Each row has its sound name in a LINK::Classes/StaticText:: on the left. That label column is as wide as the longest name. Click a sound name to select that row; click it again to clear the selection, or click another name to move it. The selected row's squares are outlined with LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-extreme2::, unless that square is also in the column currently playing. A LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt:: along the top offers LINK::Classes/AmpCommand:: and LINK::Classes/SwitchCommand::. LINK::Classes/AmpCommand:: uses the selected row's LINK::Classes/DrumStep::s that currently have a hit. CODE::amp 0:: removes those hits. LINK::Classes/SwitchCommand:: uses every LINK::Classes/DrumStep:: in that row, including empty squares. The grid sits in a LINK::Classes/ScrollView:: above the button strip, which stays put, and a scrollbar appears only when the grid is larger than that area.

Each square is a LINK::Classes/GridSlider:: held by a LINK::Classes/DrumStep::. The empty colour is colour5 and the hit colour is colour3, growing up from the bottom. The top of the square is amplitude CODE::1:: and the bottom pixel is CODE::0::. Left click or left drag turns the hit on and sets the amplitude at the pointer. Dragging back above CODE::0:: in the same gesture turns the hit on again. Dragging to CODE::0::, or a right click, turns the hit off. Each hit is a LINK::Classes/PlayableNote::. The column is a sixteenth note (start time CODE::columnIndex * 0.25:: beats) and the note lasts CODE::0.0625:: beats. MIDI is sent on channel 10. CODE::switch 1 0 0 0:: sets hit, rest, rest, rest, and then repeats, including columns that were empty. A hit created by CODE::switch:: uses velocity 100, so the bar is CODE::100/127:: of the square. An existing hit keeps its velocity. A row with no MIDI note number ignores both mouse buttons.

A strip along the bottom holds the controls. Play starts the LINK::Classes/SequencePlayer:: from beat 0. The loop runs to the last step and then wraps. A second Play while already playing does nothing. While playing, the squares in the current column are outlined with LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-extreme2::, unless that square is also in the selected row. Stop ends playback and clears that outline. Add step appends a column on the right of every row and lengthens the loop. If that column was removed earlier, its hits are shown again and play once the loop includes them. Remove step removes the rightmost column and is disabled when there are no steps. Hits in a removed column are kept. Removing the last step also stops playback. Add drum sound and Remove drum sound are hidden. Removing a row drops the hits for that drum sound.

It does not create a window. Place an instance in a LINK::Classes/Window:: layout to show it.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates an instance of TELETYPE::DrumProgrammer::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::DrumProgrammer:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

PRIVATE:: init, initClass, prAddDrumSound, prAddNote, prAddStep, prAllNotesInRow, prAppendDrumSound, prClearColumnHighlight, prClearRowSelection, prDropNotesForNoteNumber, prFindNote, prHighlightColumn, prInstallRow, prMakeButton, prMakeLabel, prMakeRow, prMakeStep, prNoteStartTime, prPlay, prRefreshRemoveButtons, prRemoveDrumSound, prRemoveNote, prRemoveStep, prSelectRow, prSelectedNotes, prSetButtonEnabled, prSortedDrumSoundNames, prStop, prSyncRowBackground, prSyncRowBorders, prSyncSequence, prSyncSquareBorder, prUpdateLoopEnd

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
(
var window = Window("Window", Rect(100, 100, 1000, 800));
window.layout = VLayout(DrumProgrammer()).margins_(0);
window.front;
)
::
